"answer": "Project Zenith is a high-priority initiative aimed at driving innovation, optimizing cloud storage, and enhancing data analytics and visualization. The project kicked off in Q3 2023 (specifically June/July) with an initial budget of $500,000 for Phase One, later approved at $2M for all phases, and a specific compliance budget of $55,000. Key leaders include Sarah Tan, Marcus Cole, and others. Major milestones include the completion of the testing phase (celebrated October 10th) and a breakthrough in predictive analytics in Phase Two. The project focuses on AI, security protocols (updated for January), and user experience, with feedback sought by the end of November and a detailed report scheduled for November 20th."
